<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deodoro da Fonseca</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as General Deodoro da Fonseca</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Deodoro da Fonseca was a Brazilian army officer who led the military <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/proclamation-of-the-republic-brazil">coup of 15 November 1889</a> that overthrew Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ii-of-brazil">Pedro II</a>. He proclaimed the republic and became the first president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/deodoro-da-fonseca.jpg" alt="Deodoro da Fonseca" width="282" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Governo do Brasil · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deodoro_da_Fonseca_(1889).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
